Tom: Yes, I read the last page last night. I really loved it.
Lucy: Me too. I thought it would be sad, but it is full of hope.
Tom: Exactly. Morrie was very ill, but he was never pessimistic.
Lucy: My favourite idea is that we should choose our own values.
Tom: Mine is that we must keep in touch with good friends.
Lucy: I am going to lend the book to my sister next week.
Tom: Good idea. Everyone should read it at least once.', '露西问汤姆读完《相约星期二》没;汤姆昨晚读完,很喜欢;露西本以为会很悲伤,结果满是希望;莫里病重却从不悲观;露西最喜欢“自己选择价值观”;汤姆最爱“要和好友保持联系”;露西下周要把书借给妹妹;汤姆说人人都该至少读一遍。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When did Tom finish the book?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Last night.","Last year.","This morning.","A month ago."]},{"q":"How did Lucy expect the book to be?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She thought it would be funny.","She thought it would be sad.","She thought it would be boring.","She thought it would be scary."]},{"q":"What is Tom''s favourite idea from the book?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Keeping in touch with good friends.","Earning lots of money.","Travelling the whole world.","Winning every game."]},{"q":"What will Lucy do next week?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Sell the book online.","Lend the book to her sister.","Throw the book away.","Write her own book."]},{"q":"What does Tom think everyone should do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Avoid the book completely.","Forget the book quickly.","Read the book at least once.","Hide the book away."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Late in his life, he was weakened by a severe illness.
Even so, he was never filled with despair.
Every Tuesday, his old student Mitch came to visit him.
Their honest talks were later turned into a famous book.', '莫里·施瓦茨曾是一位深受爱戴的大学教授;晚年被一场重病拖垮了身体;即便如此,他也从未绝望;每个星期二,他的老学生米奇都来探望;他们坦诚的谈话后来被写成了一本著名的书。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Morrie''s job?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A hospital doctor.","A news journalist.","A bus driver.","A college professor."]},{"q":"What happened to Morrie late in his life?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He became seriously ill.","He grew very rich.","He moved abroad.","He won a big prize."]},{"q":"Who visited Morrie every Tuesday?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His family doctor.","His old student Mitch.","A young reporter.","A complete stranger."]},{"q":"How did Morrie feel about his illness?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He was always very angry.","He felt nothing at all.","He never gave in to despair.","He blamed his students."]},{"q":"What were their talks later turned into?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A pop song.","A large painting.","A short film only.","A famous book."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Ben: Don''t! Where there is a will, there is a way.
Anna: But I have tried so many times already.
Ben: Remember, it is easier to succeed if you cooperate with someone.
Anna: So you mean I should ask a friend for help?
Ben: Yes. Two heads are better than one.
Anna: Thanks, Ben. I will ask Lily to study with me tonight.
Ben: Great. You will reach your dream if you stick to it.', '安娜觉得数学太难,想放弃;本说别放弃,有志者事竟成;安娜说已试了好多次;本说与人合作更容易成功;安娜问是不是该找朋友帮忙;本说是的,人多力量大;安娜决定今晚请莉莉一起学;本说只要坚持就能实现梦想。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Anna want to give up?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Maths.","Music.","Sport.","Art."]},{"q":"What proverb does Ben tell her first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Better late than never.","Where there is a will, there is a way.","Look before you leap.","Money is everything."]},{"q":"What does Ben suggest Anna do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Study completely alone.","Stop going to school.","Work together with a friend.","Copy someone''s homework."]},{"q":"Who will Anna study with tonight?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Ben.","Her teacher.","No one.","Lily."]},{"q":"What does Ben say will happen if Anna sticks to it?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She may reach her dream.","She will lose her friends.","She will surely fail.","Nothing will change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');
However, there is no upper age limit for getting a degree.
Recently, more older people have returned to study after years of work.
In one country, a man graduated from university at the age of eighty-eight.
Their stories show that it is never too late to learn.', '在多数国家,学生大约十八岁上大学;然而,攻读学位并没有年龄上限;最近,越来越多上了年纪的人在工作多年后重返校园;在某个国家,一位男士八十八岁才大学毕业;他们的故事说明,学习永远不嫌晚。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"At what age do students usually start university?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About thirty.","About eighteen.","About fifty.","About eighty."]},{"q":"Is there an upper age limit for getting a degree?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Yes, it is forty.","Yes, it is sixty.","No, there is none.","Yes, it is twenty."]},{"q":"Who has returned to study recently?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only young children.","Only school teachers.","No one at all.","More older people."]},{"q":"How old was the man who graduated in one country?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Eighty-eight.","Eighteen.","Twenty-eight.","Forty-eight."]},{"q":"What do these stories show?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only the young can learn.","It is never too late to learn.","University is useless.","Age stops all learning."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Sam: Mia! What a surprise. We were such good friends at school.
Mia: I know. I am sorry we lost touch for so long.
Sam: It is my fault too. Life just got busy after university.
Mia: Let us not lose touch again. Shall we have coffee on Saturday?
Sam: I would love that. It is important to keep in touch with old friends.
Mia: A book about friendship reminded me to find you.
Sam: Then I am grateful for that book. See you on Saturday!', '米娅惊讶地认出了十年未见的萨姆;两人曾是中学好友;米娅为长久失联而抱歉;萨姆说自己也有责任,大学后生活太忙;米娅提议周六一起喝咖啡,别再失联;萨姆欣然答应,说与老友保持联系很重要;米娅说是一本关于友谊的书让她想起去找他;萨姆说那就感谢那本书,周六见。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How long had Mia and Sam not seen each other?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["For two days.","For one month.","For ten years.","For fifty years."]},{"q":"When were Mia and Sam good friends?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["At work.","On holiday.","Online.","At school."]},{"q":"When will they meet for coffee?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["On Saturday.","On Monday.","Tonight.","Never."]},{"q":"What reminded Mia to find Sam?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A film about war.","A book about friendship.","A song about money.","A news report."]},{"q":"What does Sam say is important?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Making lots of money.","Living completely alone.","Keeping in touch with old friends.","Forgetting the past."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');
We often get distracted by small and unimportant things.
Yet each ordinary day should be treated as a gift.
Notice the people you love and tell them how you feel.
A life that is fully lived is never wasted.', '这是莫里的故事给我们的一个简单道理:我们常被琐碎而不重要的事分心;然而,每个平凡的日子都该被当作礼物;留意你所爱的人,并告诉他们你的感受;一段被充分活过的人生,绝不算虚度。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Whose story is this lesson from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A king''s story.","A sailor''s story.","A doctor''s story.","Morrie''s story."]},{"q":"What often distracts us?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Small, unimportant things.","Our closest friends.","Beautiful music.","Good books."]},{"q":"How should each ordinary day be treated?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["As a problem.","As a gift.","As a waste.","As a test."]},{"q":"What should we tell the people we love?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To leave us alone.","To work much harder.","How we feel about them.","To stay completely quiet."]},{"q":"What kind of life is never wasted?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A life spent worrying.","A life of pure laziness.","A life without any friends.","A life that is fully lived."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'fltrp');

